          "intro": "Read these supplied proposals:\n```text\nRequirement: initial new-version traffic <=10%; extra capacity <= one full workload; retain a return route to known-good.\nRolling: first batch 25%; extra capacity one batch; replace changed portions to return.\nBlue/green: switch 100%; extra capacity one full workload; switch back to retained old environment.\nCanary: initial 10%; extra capacity 10% workload; route back to retained known-good.\n```\n\n**Response slots—not delivery evidence.**\n\nOnly the Workload response-slot column is displayed. Use the following row-to-judgement mapping:\nSelect row \"orders\" to submit this judgement: Canary: limited initial traffic exposure fits the bound, its supplied extra capacity fits the limit, and traffic can return to the retained known-good version. The rolling first batch and blue/green traffic switch exceed the exposure bound.\nSelect row \"support\" to submit this judgement: Blue/green: a return route makes the 100% switch meet the 10% bound.\nSelect row \"unallocated\" to submit this judgement: Rolling: progressive replacement necessarily means at most 10% initial traffic.",
          "tasks": [
